> Why can this code cause a race condition?               

⏺ Two goroutines write `count` without a lock, so
  updates can interleave and be lost.

You
 Refactor the worker pool so that:                        
 - jobs are cancelled on shutdown                         
 - errors are collected and returned                      

Claude
 Here is the updated Stop method:
  ```go
  func (p *Pool) Stop(ctx context.Context) error {
      close(p.jobs)
      return p.waitCtx(ctx)
  }
  ```

